# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the CPU, memory, and GPU resources for a managed workflow, and define sizes that match the size of the problem."
msgstr "Scegli le risorse di CPU, memoria e GPU per un workflow gestito e definisci dimensioni adatte alla dimensione del problema."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile"
msgstr "Scegli un profilo di calcolo"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile {#choose-a-compute-profile}"
msgstr "Scegli un profilo di calcolo {#choose-a-compute-profile}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Managed workflows run on compute profiles. A compute profile is a fixed combination of vCPUs, memory, and GPUs, similar to the resources that you request from an HPC scheduler. When you upload a workflow, you map its sizes, such as `S` and `M`, to profiles, and each run picks one of those sizes. The job then runs on its own node with that profile, and keeps the profile until the job ends.\n"
msgstr "I workflow gestiti vengono eseguiti su profili di calcolo. Un profilo di calcolo è una combinazione fissa di vCPU, memoria e GPU, simile alle risorse che richiedi a uno scheduler HPC. Quando carichi un workflow, associ le sue dimensioni, come `S` e `M`, ai profili, e ogni esecuzione sceglie una di queste dimensioni. Il job viene quindi eseguito su un proprio nodo con quel profilo e lo mantiene fino alla fine del job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Profile | vCPUs | Memory (GB) | GPUs |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | None |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | None |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | None |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | None |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Profilo | vCPU | Memoria (GB) | GPU |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | Nessuna |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | Nessuna |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | Nessuna |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | Nessuna |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A profile ID has the form `{cpu}x{memory}`, with memory in GB, or `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` for a profile with GPUs. For example, `24x120x1l40s` has 24 vCPUs, 120 GB of memory, and one NVIDIA L40S GPU.\n"
msgstr "L'ID di un profilo ha la forma `{cpu}x{memory}`, con la memoria in GB, oppure `{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` per un profilo con GPU. Ad esempio, `24x120x1l40s` ha 24 vCPU, 120 GB di memoria e una GPU NVIDIA L40S.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check available profiles {#check-available-profiles}"
msgstr "Controlla i profili disponibili {#check-available-profiles}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see which profiles are available, call `compute_profiles()`:\n"
msgstr "Per vedere quali profili sono disponibili, chiama `compute_profiles()`:\n"

